1
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,100
Why are you crying?

2
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:39,033
If you want to play, just play.

3
00:00:41,433 --> 00:00:44,167
No. Let's go, Arisa-chan.

4
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:47,267
Are you sure?

5
00:00:47,767 --> 00:00:48,867
You were so good.

6
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:55,600
Because I can't play anymore.

7
00:01:02,467 --> 00:01:04,233
Hey, I don't get this. Where is it?

8
00:01:05,167 --> 00:01:08,367
- It's 26 and 39.
- Huh? Isn't that long?

9
00:01:08,367 --> 00:01:09,033
Right?

10
00:01:10,267 --> 00:01:11,133
Nice.

11
00:01:14,867 --> 00:01:17,933
Hayama, the test's about to start.

12
00:01:17,933 --> 00:01:18,867
What are you doing?

13
00:01:24,233 --> 00:01:26,067
I was just thinking how pretty the light is.

14
00:01:28,167 --> 00:01:31,567
You know, I've always thought...

15
00:01:32,067 --> 00:01:33,767
you're like a baby.

16
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:36,233
Huh? A baby?

17
00:01:37,167 --> 00:01:40,300
Oh, I totally get that.
Hayama-kun is kind of babyish.

18
00:01:43,267 --> 00:01:44,333
What do you mean, a baby?

19
00:01:45,533 --> 00:01:46,600
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffy.

20
00:01:47,567 --> 00:01:50,600
There, there, there.
Aww, those sparkly eyes.

21
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:52,733
So cute.

22
00:01:59,067 --> 00:02:01,033
Are you treating me like a baby now?

23
00:02:02,033 --> 00:02:02,533
Huh?

24
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:05,467
Phew, thank goodness.

25
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:09,567
- I dodged a failing grade!
- I lost.

26
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:12,333
Oh, the results are up.

27
00:02:13,367 --> 00:02:15,900
Whoa, Ao got first place!

28
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:19,100
Top of the entrance class
really is different.

29
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:21,067
- Oh, Arisa-san.
- Yeah.

30
00:02:21,067 --> 00:02:22,433
What rank did you get?

31
00:02:23,233 --> 00:02:26,367
- 24th.
- Whoa, that's pretty high!

32
00:02:33,467 --> 00:02:37,733
That's how Midori-kun and I first met.

33
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:46,167
♪

34
00:02:46,167 --> 00:02:50,267
♪

35
00:02:50,767 --> 00:02:53,933
♪

36
00:02:53,933 --> 00:02:55,567
♪

37
00:02:55,567 --> 00:03:01,433
♪

38
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:04,400
♪

39
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:09,900
♪

40
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:11,233
♪

41
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:17,833
♪

42
00:03:17,833 --> 00:03:19,767
♪

43
00:03:36,233 --> 00:03:36,733
Ao.

44
00:03:37,967 --> 00:03:39,400
They said there's a relay at the end.

45
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,733
Oh, really?

46
00:03:40,733 --> 00:03:43,900
- You've been picked as a runner, Ao.
- Me?

47
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:46,100
Well, you're fast.

48
00:03:48,467 --> 00:03:50,800
We can't lose to Class 1
no matter what.

49
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:53,767
What's that? Revenge for the test?

50
00:03:54,267 --> 00:03:55,833
I can't wait until finals.

51
00:03:56,567 --> 00:03:58,300
This is how I'll make up for it.

52
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:02,600
- Apparently Class 3 is stacking its team
with track club guys.
- Seriously?

53
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:04,167
That's so childish.

54
00:04:04,567 --> 00:04:06,767
Apparently someone's got a rivalry
thing going with Ao.

55
00:04:06,767 --> 00:04:07,433
Huh? Me?

56
00:04:07,867 --> 00:04:10,200
Yeah, I heard it from someone in Class 3.

57
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:13,367
A guy named Yamamura lost to Ao
on the test,

58
00:04:13,367 --> 00:04:14,533
and he's holding a grudge.

59
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:15,667
Yamamura?

60
00:04:17,132 --> 00:04:18,800
Ooh, nice!

61
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:19,933
Go blow him away, Ao!

62
00:04:20,367 --> 00:04:23,133
'Blow him away'? That's scary, Arisa-chan.

63
00:04:23,133 --> 00:04:26,500
Well, good luck. Good luck.

64
00:04:29,967 --> 00:04:31,833
It feels so nice out today.

65
00:04:32,633 --> 00:04:35,900
I'd rather soak up the sun
than run a relay.

66
00:04:39,100 --> 00:04:40,100
Midori-kun, think you can do it?

67
00:04:40,833 --> 00:04:41,367
Easy.

68
00:04:42,767 --> 00:04:43,267
Alright.

69
00:04:45,133 --> 00:04:46,133
And he dashes to the finish!

70
00:04:51,467 --> 00:04:51,967
Ah.

71
00:04:54,833 --> 00:04:56,867
The wind feels amazing.

72
00:05:00,833 --> 00:05:01,767
Running...

73
00:05:04,267 --> 00:05:05,833
...feels good.

74
00:05:08,567 --> 00:05:10,000
It really feels good.

75
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:24,367
What?

76
00:05:30,933 --> 00:05:32,133
That felt great.

77
00:05:32,833 --> 00:05:35,400
I talked big, and then I got passed.

78
00:05:36,433 --> 00:05:39,633
I made you train with me, Master,
and then made you feel bad, too.

79
00:05:41,900 --> 00:05:42,900
I'm really sorry.

80
00:05:45,967 --> 00:05:49,133
- Well, we realized we weren't practicing enough, either.
- Ao?

81
00:05:49,967 --> 00:05:54,000
- What's wrong?
- Yeah. We really do have to run properly.

82
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,067
That's cool.

83
00:05:55,933 --> 00:05:56,433
Huh?

84
00:05:58,533 --> 00:05:59,500
Admitting your own flaws,

85
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,233
and really owning up to them.

86
00:06:11,867 --> 00:06:13,400
Hey, hey, Hayama.

87
00:06:15,167 --> 00:06:15,767
What?

88
00:06:16,067 --> 00:06:17,267
Can't you eat onions?

89
00:06:18,133 --> 00:06:19,033
Hey, Yoshida.

90
00:06:19,767 --> 00:06:20,267
Huh?

91
00:06:20,367 --> 00:06:22,300
Well, you're curious about Midori-kun,
aren't you?

92
00:06:24,233 --> 00:06:25,633
Midori-kun...

93
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:35,900
What kind of person is he, I wonder.

94
00:06:41,367 --> 00:06:43,733
You can just call me Midori.

95
00:06:44,767 --> 00:06:45,267
Huh?

96
00:06:45,933 --> 00:06:46,433
Really?

97
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:50,533
Why do you look so happy about it?

98
00:06:50,533 --> 00:06:54,467
Oh, it just feels like
we've gotten closer.

99
00:06:54,467 --> 00:06:56,467
That makes me happy.

100
00:06:58,233 --> 00:06:59,167
What's wrong?

101
00:07:01,967 --> 00:07:03,600
No, it's nothing.

102
00:07:04,533 --> 00:07:10,067
Okay. Well, good luck at practice.

103
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:15,133
Midori-kun... see you.

104
00:07:20,100 --> 00:07:21,067
He smiled at me.

105
00:07:32,267 --> 00:07:33,300
What are you doing?

106
00:07:34,333 --> 00:07:39,467
- Midori-kun.
- What high schooler plays with his own shadow?

107
00:07:39,467 --> 00:07:41,600
I wasn't playing.
I was just looking.

108
00:07:42,233 --> 00:07:44,067
Whatever.

109
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:53,400
Midori-kun, do you compete in meets?

110
00:07:54,467 --> 00:07:55,400
Oh, with the club?

111
00:07:56,767 --> 00:07:57,433
Yeah, I do.

112
00:07:58,300 --> 00:07:59,000
I see.

113
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:03,367
Hey, can I come watch your next meet?

114
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,100
Huh?

115
00:08:05,133 --> 00:08:05,733
Why?

116
00:08:06,467 --> 00:08:08,033
Because I want to see you run, Midori-kun.

117
00:08:08,433 --> 00:08:10,167
But you were faster than me.

118
00:08:10,167 --> 00:08:11,600
That doesn't matter.

119
00:08:17,367 --> 00:08:19,400
I guess that's fine.

120
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:20,833
Yes!

121
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,267
What a cutie.

122
00:08:27,567 --> 00:08:28,933
Huh?

123
00:08:28,933 --> 00:08:29,567
What did you say?

124
00:08:30,833 --> 00:08:31,333
Huh?

125
00:08:32,299 --> 00:08:34,200
Never mind. Don't ask me to repeat it.

126
00:08:34,667 --> 00:08:35,667
It was an insult.

127
00:08:36,232 --> 00:08:36,732
Huh?

128
00:08:37,467 --> 00:08:38,467
You insulted me?

129
00:08:39,332 --> 00:08:39,900
What did you say?

130
00:08:40,633 --> 00:08:41,667
Shut up, shut up!

131
00:08:42,667 --> 00:08:43,600
Seriously?

132
00:08:51,833 --> 00:08:53,000
No way.

133
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:58,367
Look, it really is the onions.

134
00:09:01,067 --> 00:09:04,800
- Well, they almost make you cry.
- Why's that?

135
00:09:05,867 --> 00:09:06,667
Seriously.

136
00:09:10,367 --> 00:09:11,533
I'll take care of it. Let's go.

137
00:09:15,467 --> 00:09:16,167
Wait.

138
00:09:21,133 --> 00:09:24,467
- Man, that guy was so cool.
- Totally.

139
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:27,200
He was so, so cool.

140
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:28,433
So what happened after that?

141
00:09:28,933 --> 00:09:32,133
- I couldn't get his contact info.
- What?

142
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:35,200
- Why not?
- Because...

143
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:37,933
We only met the other day!

144
00:09:37,933 --> 00:09:38,967
I only just found him, you know.

145
00:09:40,900 --> 00:09:43,333
Man, he was so cool.

146
00:09:43,333 --> 00:09:44,000
Right? He was cool, wasn't he?

147
00:09:45,233 --> 00:09:45,767
Ah!

148
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:48,200
It's Midori-kun!

149
00:09:50,733 --> 00:09:52,233
Midori-kun?

150
00:09:52,467 --> 00:09:53,000
Yamamura?

151
00:09:53,933 --> 00:09:55,700
The guy who lost to Ao in the relay.

152
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:57,867
What, did you two become friends?

153
00:09:59,333 --> 00:10:02,233
I don't know if we're friends, exactly.

154
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:04,933
Did he do something to you?

155
00:10:05,567 --> 00:10:07,767
- Want me to blow him away?
- Don't blow him away!

156
00:10:08,467 --> 00:10:11,167
It's okay. He's a good guy.

157
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:14,433
Ah.

158
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:19,200
He's so cute when he smiles.

159
00:10:25,367 --> 00:10:26,667
Ao.

160
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:30,533
Could it be...

161
00:10:36,433 --> 00:10:37,767
Shima-chan.

162
00:10:38,567 --> 00:10:40,367
Arisa-chan.

163
00:10:42,133 --> 00:10:44,433
Wait, no way.

164
00:10:46,967 --> 00:10:51,033
Maybe so.

165
00:10:51,033 --> 00:10:54,500
No, no, no. L-love?

166
00:10:54,867 --> 00:10:55,367
Huh?

167
00:10:55,733 --> 00:10:58,533
But they say the best day to start
is the day you decide to.

168
00:10:58,533 --> 00:11:00,367
No, no, no. It's way too soon.

169
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:03,433
Besides,

170
00:11:04,167 --> 00:11:07,400
Midori-kun probably isn't like that.

171
00:11:10,733 --> 00:11:13,033
Hmm, true.

172
00:11:13,033 --> 00:11:15,333
- Who knows?
- Hmm.

173
00:11:16,267 --> 00:11:17,767
Hmm, hmm.

174
00:12:01,633 --> 00:12:03,267
I'm done with the piano.

175
00:12:03,933 --> 00:12:04,733
I don't need it anymore.

176
00:12:13,967 --> 00:12:14,467
Once again,

177
00:12:16,133 --> 00:12:17,467
I give up.

178
00:12:26,900 --> 00:12:29,000
Um, Midori-kun, would you have lunch
with me?

179
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,533
Midori-kun, Midori-kun.

180
00:12:31,733 --> 00:12:32,733
Midori-kun, would you have lunch

181
00:12:32,733 --> 00:12:34,033
with me?

182
00:12:35,333 --> 00:12:36,767
Midori-kun.

183
00:12:41,733 --> 00:12:43,133
Um, Midori-kun...

184
00:12:43,667 --> 00:12:44,433
Hayama?

185
00:13:02,567 --> 00:13:04,433
Midori-kun's eyelashes...

186
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:14,733
What?

187
00:13:17,333 --> 00:13:19,133
Nothing.

188
00:13:32,067 --> 00:13:33,833
Still unable to give up,

189
00:13:34,667 --> 00:13:35,867
I started my third year.

190
00:13:39,067 --> 00:13:41,900
Ugh, it's nothing but assignments
every single day.

191
00:13:43,967 --> 00:13:46,333
Lucky you. Entrance exams
are no problem for you.

192
00:13:46,767 --> 00:13:48,733
That's not true.

193
00:13:49,267 --> 00:13:51,533
I wonder what Yamamura's plans are
after graduation.

194
00:13:52,033 --> 00:13:54,667
Yeah, I wonder. Maybe he'll go to
a university up in Tohoku?

195
00:13:55,067 --> 00:13:56,900
Oh, I heard it's a university in Tokyo.

196
00:13:57,633 --> 00:14:00,833
Hmm, I see. Then we can still see him
after graduation.

197
00:14:02,233 --> 00:14:05,200
- I don't know if we'll actually get to.
- Why?

198
00:14:05,833 --> 00:14:07,467
You're aiming for a Tokyo university
too, right, Ao?

199
00:14:09,333 --> 00:14:11,667
But I'm not even that close to him.

200
00:14:11,667 --> 00:14:13,033
That's not true.

201
00:14:13,033 --> 00:14:15,567
You've had lunch with him
once in a while, haven't you?

202
00:14:15,567 --> 00:14:19,733
- Yeah, exactly.
- You even went to watch his club meet, didn't you?

203
00:14:20,867 --> 00:14:23,300
But we were in different classes
all three years.

204
00:14:24,033 --> 00:14:26,833
In the end, I'm just one of the crowd,
you know?

205
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:30,267
Hmm. And I never even got
his contact info.

206
00:14:33,333 --> 00:14:34,933
Ugh, you're being so negative.

207
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:38,667
- He gets down more easily than you'd think.
- Hmm.

208
00:14:38,667 --> 00:14:39,433
Ah.

209
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:47,900
Once we graduate, I won't be able
to see him every day.

210
00:14:50,233 --> 00:14:50,967
You looking at me?

211
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:52,767
Looking at what?

212
00:15:08,167 --> 00:15:11,833
- Don't stare at people's faces.
- Sorry.

213
00:15:12,933 --> 00:15:16,533
Weirdo. Here, my textbook.

214
00:15:16,533 --> 00:15:17,933
Oh, thanks.

215
00:15:18,967 --> 00:15:20,900
Sorry, I forgot mine.

216
00:15:22,900 --> 00:15:25,800
Can't be helped. You're a baby.

217
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:27,667
I'm not a baby.

218
00:15:27,667 --> 00:15:29,167
Yes, you are.

219
00:15:45,633 --> 00:15:47,500
Hey, Midori-kun.

220
00:15:49,767 --> 00:15:50,267
Hm?

221
00:15:55,267 --> 00:15:56,767
After graduation,

222
00:16:06,967 --> 00:16:08,800
we'll be college students.

223
00:16:15,700 --> 00:16:18,467
Well, if we get in.

224
00:16:30,567 --> 00:16:35,800
Hey, Midori-kun, the teacher
was calling for you.

225
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:40,733
Yeah. See you.

226
00:16:41,567 --> 00:16:42,067
Yeah.

227
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:48,967
Hayama,

228
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:52,433
are you okay with this?

229
00:16:53,033 --> 00:16:54,733
Just graduating like this?

230
00:16:59,333 --> 00:16:59,933
What do you mean?

231
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:05,067
Forget it if you don't get it.

232
00:18:00,367 --> 00:18:02,033
Right when I wake up in the morning,

233
00:18:04,233 --> 00:18:08,167
I wish I could see Midori-kun's eyelashes.

234
00:18:47,933 --> 00:18:52,567
♪

235
00:18:54,333 --> 00:18:57,433
♪

236
00:18:57,433 --> 00:19:04,200
Don't you want to talk to Yamamura?

237
00:19:04,433 --> 00:19:07,933
♪

238
00:19:07,933 --> 00:19:10,200
Are you sure you won't regret
leaving things like this?

239
00:19:12,700 --> 00:19:18,667
♪

240
00:19:18,667 --> 00:19:24,300
♪

241
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:26,767
♪

242
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:32,400
♪

243
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:36,033
♪

244
00:19:36,033 --> 00:19:39,400
♪

245
00:19:41,100 --> 00:19:46,267
♪

246
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:47,300
Ah.

247
00:19:53,533 --> 00:19:55,033
Well then, Midori-kun.

248
00:19:55,033 --> 00:19:56,333
We're heading on ahead.

249
00:19:56,867 --> 00:19:59,433
On your marks... alright, let's go!

250
00:20:05,867 --> 00:20:06,367
Hey.

251
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:10,933
You know,

252
00:20:14,867 --> 00:20:16,367
because you were there, Midori-kun,

253
00:20:19,433 --> 00:20:21,433
school was fun.

254
00:20:25,967 --> 00:20:27,400
Because I was there?

255
00:20:30,367 --> 00:20:31,633
Yeah.

256
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:39,667
Thank you, really.

257
00:20:51,833 --> 00:20:52,967
Well...

258
00:20:57,567 --> 00:20:59,067
See you.

259
00:21:12,167 --> 00:21:13,167
Hayama.

260
00:21:20,633 --> 00:21:22,800
Don't you have

261
00:21:24,833 --> 00:21:26,767
anything to say to me?

262
00:21:31,933 --> 00:21:32,733
Oh.

263
00:21:34,700 --> 00:21:35,933
I do.

264
00:21:45,433 --> 00:21:47,767
Even after we graduate,

265
00:21:52,233 --> 00:21:54,567
could we meet up sometimes?

266
00:22:04,667 --> 00:22:05,700
Sure, I guess.

267
00:22:07,533 --> 00:22:08,667
It's just meeting up.

268
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:14,933
Yes!

269
00:22:20,500 --> 00:22:22,000
Until the very end,

270
00:22:23,067 --> 00:22:24,833
I never knew what Midori-kun

271
00:22:25,700 --> 00:22:26,800
really thought of me.

272
00:22:31,167 --> 00:22:31,667
So...

273
00:22:34,600 --> 00:22:35,767
Contact info and...

274
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:37,500
Oh.

275
00:22:38,067 --> 00:22:38,567
Yeah.

276
00:22:41,800 --> 00:22:42,533
Here.

277
00:22:42,900 --> 00:22:43,400
Yeah.

278
00:22:48,833 --> 00:22:50,167
What's with this sticker?

279
00:22:51,667 --> 00:22:52,833
It's my favorite.

280
00:22:54,367 --> 00:22:55,000
But,

281
00:22:55,833 --> 00:22:57,600
if he'll still meet me after graduation,

282
00:22:58,400 --> 00:23:00,700
I don't think he hates me.

283
00:23:02,167 --> 00:23:03,100
That's enough for me.

284
00:23:10,667 --> 00:23:14,167
- I'm still happy I get to see you like this, Midori-kun.
- Friends, huh?

285
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:17,433
Actually, there's a girl who says
she's interested in you.

286
00:23:17,433 --> 00:23:18,633
I'd like to get closer to her.

287
00:23:18,933 --> 00:23:21,700
At the very least, I could get
a girlfriend, right?

288
00:23:22,767 --> 00:23:23,433
I don't like that.
